# INTERVenE Source Code

This archive accompanies an anonymized submission currently under double-blind review.

It contains the complete implementation used in the experiments reported in the paper, including the INTERVenE models, symbolic temporal abstraction pipeline (KBTA-Mediator), and baseline implementations (GRU-D, STRATS, KARMALEGO).

---

## Repository Structure

```
code/
│
├── INTERVenE/
│   ├── encoder/
│   └── decoder/
│
├── KBTA-Mediator/
│
├── KarmaLego/
│
└── baselines/
```

### INTERVenE

Contains the proposed models introduced in the paper.

- **encoder/** — INTERVenE-Enc implementation
- **decoder/** — INTERVenE-Ar implementation

Each submodule is fully self-contained and can be installed and executed independently. Dependencies, configuration files, and training scripts are local to each submodule.

### Mediator

Knowledge-based Temporal Abstraction (KBTA) engine used to convert raw clinical events into symbolic temporal intervals, including the diabetes knowledge base that handles the full abstraction.

### KarmaLego

Symbolic temporal pattern mining baseline used in the experimental comparison + ML pipeline from mining to prediction.

### baselines

Implementations of the remaining NN baseline models evaluated in the paper.

---

# Installation

Each repository behaves as an independent Python module.

Please refer to the README contained within each subdirectory for installation instructions, required dependencies, documentation and API.

No shared installation step is required between repositories.

---

# Data

Experiments were performed using the MIMIC-IV database.

The dataset is not redistributed with this submission due to licensing restrictions.

Users must obtain access through the official MIMIC-IV credentialing process and construct the cohort described in the paper.

raw mimic -> MIMIC-Dataset-ETL -> KBTA-Mediator -> KarmaLego+INTERVenE
                    |
                other NN baselines     

---

# Reproducing the Paper

The archive contains all code required to reproduce the experiments reported in the manuscript.

Specifically it includes:

- INTERVenE encoder and decoder implementations
- Knowledge-based temporal abstraction pipeline
- Baseline implementations
- Training scripts
- Evaluation scripts
- Configuration files

The exact experimental protocol, hyperparameters, and preprocessing pipeline are described in the paper and supplementary material. Final hyperparameters are hardcoded in configuration files attached.

---

# Anonymity

This archive has been prepared for anonymous peer review.

Repository metadata and identifying information have been removed for the review process.

Complete project history and public repository links will be restored upon publication.
